WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.812
In this video, we'll move the setup
chat into the Excalidraw case study,

2
00:00:09.812 --> 00:00:14.636
run it on localhost, and open it
in the browser inside VS Code.

3
00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:17.928
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

4
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.470
The setup chat already knows where the
case study is, so one prompt does it all.

5
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.819
It asks how to bring the chat over.
Use the existing folder, the simplest choice.

6
00:00:35.282 --> 00:00:37.668
Now the chat moves out of Chats and into

7
00:00:37.668 --> 00:00:40.293
the case study's workspace, history and all.

8
00:00:40.293 --> 00:00:41.725
That's a session moving.

9
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.951
It starts the app on
localhost, and opens it in

10
00:00:46.951 --> 00:00:50.103
the integrated browser,
right next to the chat.

11
00:00:55.837 --> 00:01:01.501
While it loads, open the practice brief,
brief.md, in your copy's workshop folder.

12
00:01:06.787 --> 00:01:11.050
It's fictional user testing on
the toolbar: six first-time users,

13
00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.050
and what tripped them up,
written as problems, not solutions.

14
00:01:16.087 --> 00:01:21.638
Icons without words. A lock nobody understood.
Tools hidden behind three dots.

15
00:01:21.638 --> 00:01:25.836
And after every shape,
the toolbar jumps back to the arrow.

16
00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:31.065
Next, we'll mark up the toolbar,
and fix the most confusing part.
